  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Usg obligated $1.2B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 49 awards, with an average award size of $23.8M and obligations up 56.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $67.6M in FY21 to $1.2B in FY26, with notable steps at $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $745M in FY25. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.1B, followed by the Department of State at $18M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $12.1M. Custom Computer Programming Services is Palantir Usg's largest market at $1B, supplemented by Software Publishers at $124M and Other Management Consulting Services at $27.1M. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date, and the note specifies that award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values while the rest are obligations. This snapshot highlights where federal dollars flowed to Palantir Usg through the fiscal year to date and which markets and agencies accounted for the majority of obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Palantir Usg's federal obligations change over time?",
        "body": "Palantir Usg's obligations rose to $1.2B in FY26 from $745M in FY25, representing obligations up 56.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year increase from $67.6M in FY21 to $1.2B in FY26, with intermediate levels of $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, and $288M in FY24. The FY2026 total is fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Palantir Usg's largest federal customers and which markets dominate?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $1.1B in obligations, followed by the Department of State at $18M and NASA at $12.1M. Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest market at $1B, with Software Publishers at $124M and Other Management Consulting Services at $27.1M also significant."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Palantir Usg make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Palantir Usg has $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Palantir Usg received those obligations across 49 awards, with an average award size of $23.8M and obligations up 56.7% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Palantir Usg?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, the Department of State, NASA, and the U.S. International Development Finance Corporation buy from Palantir Usg. The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B, the Department of State obligated $18M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $12.1M, and the U.S. International Development Finance Corporation obligated $8.1M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Palantir Usg sell to the government?",
      "a": "Palantir Usg sells software and related services to the government, led by Custom Computer Programming Services and Software Publishers. Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $1B, Software Publishers accounts for $124M, Other Management Consulting Services accounts for $27.1M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $247K, and an additional Software Publishers entry accounts for $236K."
